=========================================================
          ELASTICSEARCH INTERVIEW NOTES
=========================================================

Q. What is Elasticsearch?

Distributed Search Engine.

Stores JSON Documents.

Built on Apache Lucene.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. What is Index?

Like Database.

Example

linux-logs

----------------------------------------------------

Q. What is Document?

JSON Record stored inside Index.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. What is Cluster?

Collection of Elasticsearch Nodes.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. What is Node?

Single Elasticsearch Server.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Difference between Cluster Name and Node Name?

Cluster Name

Logical Cluster Identifier

Node Name

Logical Server Identifier

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Primary Shard?

Original Data.

Each document first goes into Primary Shard.

Only Primary accepts write operation.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Replica Shard?

Copy of Primary Shard.

Provides

High Availability

Read Performance

No write operation directly.

----------------------------------------------------

Example

Index

5 Primary

1 Replica

Result

5 Primary

5 Replica

Total

10 Shards

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Why Replica?

Node Failure

High Availability

Load Balancing

Read Scaling

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Can Replica exist without Primary?

NO

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Can Primary exist without Replica?

YES

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Default Replica?

Normally

1

Can be changed.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Why Cluster Health Yellow?

Replica not allocated.

Mostly happens in Single Node Cluster.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Green Cluster?

Everything allocated.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Red Cluster?

Primary Shards Missing.

Data unavailable.

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Difference between 9200 and 9300?

9200

REST API

Client Communication

9300

Internal Node Communication

----------------------------------------------------

Q. What is Heap?

Java Memory

Configured in

jvm.options

----------------------------------------------------

Q. Why Same Xms and Xmx?

Avoid JVM Heap Resizing.

Better Performance.

=========================================================
